This project uses the @omni-design/components design system.

Read node_modules/@omni-design/components/CLAUDE.md before writing any UI.
It is the contract; the rules below are the ones most often broken.
Component props (types, allowed values, defaults, parents, examples):
docs/API.md — read it instead of opening dist/.
Long form, for anything CLAUDE.md does not cover: docs/REFERENCE.md.
If the project has the studio's CLAUDE.md / DINO-TOKENS.md for its design
system, that file names the system's own background, bars, buttons and cards.

SETUP
- npm install @omni-design/components @omni-design/icons @mui/material@^7
  @emotion/react @emotion/styled   (MUI 7 — MUI 9 breaks the build)
- Wrap the app in <OmniDesignProvider themeURL={…}>: your design system's
  theme.json URL, or OMNI_DEFAULT_THEME_URL (exported) for the package theme.
  Do not import the CSS files yourself; the provider loads them in order.

COMPONENTS
- Import every UI element from '@omni-design/components'. No raw <button>,
  <input>, <select>, <input type="range">, <h1>-<h6>, <p>, or <a href>, and
  no '@mui/material' imports. Icons come from '@omni-design/icons'
  (import HomeIcon from '@omni-design/icons/Home'), not '@mui/icons-material'.
- Missing component? Tag it — // MISSING-LIB-COMPONENT: <Name> — never fake
  one with a styled <div>.
- Anything that floats (account panels, hover cards) is <Popover>. A menu is
  <Dropdown><MenuButton/><Menu><MenuItem/></Menu></Dropdown> — Menu alone
  renders nothing, and it does not portal (inside a clipped area use Popover).
- Segmented choice: <ToggleButtonGroup> (ButtonGroup is plain buttons).
  Tabs that go to pages: <Tabs navigation> (a Tab drops href otherwise).
  A Card with href is a real link. Status messages: <Alert color>.
- Code, shell commands, copyable URLs: <CodeBlock code language>.
- Icon-only button: aria-label on the Button, none on the icon.

COLOR AND SURFACES
- Never write hex colors or hard-coded radii. Use tokens.
- To paint a region use <Section theme surface> (or data-theme +
  data-surface); <ThemedZone> sets the attributes without painting.
  Never background: var(--Surface) / var(--Container) / a hex.
- Themes: Default, Primary, Secondary, Tertiary, Neutral, Info, Success,
  Warning, Error, App-Bar, Nav-Bar, Status. Default is the designer's page
  background. There are NO -Light / -Medium / -Dark themes or button / chip /
  badge variants — lighter/darker is a surface level.
- Surfaces: Surface-Dimmest, Surface-Dim, Surface, Surface-Bright,
  Surface-Brightest; cards: Container-Lowest, Container-Low, Container,
  Container-High, Container-Highest.
- Bars use data-theme="App-Bar" (top bar, side rail) and "Nav-Bar" (phone
  bottom bar); AppBar / BottomNavigation set it themselves. Never pick a
  palette for navigation.
- Never pass style={{ color, background }} to a library component; use its
  variant or color prop. Body has no bold — use <Subtitle>.
- Use all three color roles: mostly Default/Primary, one or two Secondary
  sections, Tertiary only as accents (never a section). Colored text is the
  color prop (primary/secondary/tertiary). Eyebrow colors itself.
- Links do not change color on hover; do not add one.
- Shadows: components pick them. Floating/fixed things cast black shadows
  (--Effect-Level-N-Neutral); things on a surface keep the tinted
  --Effect-Level-N.

DEVICES
- Type follows the screen through the theme's CSS. Do not set data-device
  (it only pins a device on purpose).
- A site nav is <AppBar navLinks endSlot> — it collapses below 900px by
  itself. App navigation (rail + bottom bar) comes from the Adaptive Nav
  add-on's exported file, not hand-assembled.

LAYOUT
- Never center a container's text to center components inside it —
  text-align is inherited and centers their text too. Center the box.
